{"full":"hf:ysharma/OPF-Image-Anonymizer","spaceId":"ysharma/OPF-Image-Anonymizer","name":"OPF Image Anonymizer","source":"huggingface","description":"Use OAI's Privacy Filter to redact PII info from any image","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","topics":["gradio","region:us"],"technologies":["Python"],"likes":19,"created":"2026-04-22T07:59:28.000Z","updated":"2026-04-23T16:56:40.000Z","license":"apache-2.0","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://ysharma-opf-image-anonymizer.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/ysharma/OPF-Image-Anonymizer","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:19.219Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:19.219Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:29:19.219Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🦀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Drop in a screenshot of a chat, email, or document or any image for that matter. The app runs OCR, feeds the recognised text through OpenAI Privacy Filter, maps detected PII spans back to their original pixel positions, and overlays black bars in a canvas editor. Toggle, move, add or delete bars — then save a ready-for-Twitter PNG or copy it straight to the clipboard."],"features":["OCR + privacy filter in one pass: Tesseract extracts word-level boxes, the filter model finds PII char spans, the backend unions the two into redaction rectangles.","Canvas editor: not expressible with gr.Blocks but possible with gr.Server. Drag to draw bars, click to select, drag to move, Delete to remove. Paste from clipboard to upload.","Eight PII categories: Person, Address, Email, Phone, URL, Date, Account Number, Secret — each toggleable from the sidebar.","Export locally: download as PNG or copy to clipboard. No upload of edits, no server round-trip."],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/ysharma/OPF-Image-Anonymizer/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d08a2cf6da7596241ba8d0cf9ec37409463219b0687e004c36ff0905343d1532","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T17:10:47.2